{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> The sense of \"for YHWH brought you out\" — because you said, \"You brought us out\" — and behold, two signs He will perform for you, that you may know that He brought you out: one in the evening of this day, and the second tomorrow morning. And it should have been \"in the evening and in the morning you shall know,\" for [the verse] does not join \"and in the morning\" with \"and you shall see the glory of YHWH,\" for on the very day they saw the glory, as he will explain."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Resolved the ambiguous כי at the opening as introducing the reason for the two signs; the syntax is compressed and the second כי clause is rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:02.709541488Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}